  {
   "type": "cols",
   "layout": "33-66",
   "columns": [
    [
     {
      "type": "textmedia",
      "header": "<h1> FAQ </h1>",
      "body": "<p>Frequently asked questions</p>",
      "images": [],
      "videos": [],
      "pos": "text",
      "cols": 1,
      "valign": "top",
      "ftype": "text",
      "id": "c1799",
      "bg": "",
      "space": {
       "before": "default",
       "after": "default"
      }
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "type": "accordion",
      "header": "",
      "items": [
       {
        "title": "Why are there different camera variants?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Depending on the tool dimensions and types to be inspected, ZOLLER offers three different camera technologies »pomBasic« three different camera technologies. This means that every customer receives a solution that is optimally tailored to their requirements.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1796",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Are the devices user-friendly?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Yes, »pomBasic« is characterized by a high level of user-friendliness, among many other advantages. For example, the most important and most frequently used functions can be arranged in favorite groups. This means that every operator has quick and simple access to the required measuring functions.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1794",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Does the »pomBasic« the option of zooming in on cross-sectional views using the digital zoom?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>A digital zoom is available in the operating software for all camera variants. In addition, the cameras of the variants »pomColorCam« and »pomMicroCam« have an optical zoom.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1792",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Are DXF comparisons supported for all devices in the »pomBasic«-Series supported?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The DXF function can be used to quickly and reliably align tools optically with their nominal contour in DXF format.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1790",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Are there options for quick illumination settings for Incident light and transmitted light?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>A function for automatic illumination setting at the touch of a button is available for Incident light. In addition, all available illuminations can be quickly and simply optimally adjusted using the quick access function.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1788",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "When do I need a standard camera (»pomBasic«) or a micro camera („pomBasic MTI)?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Ideally, the diameter range of the »pomBasic« starts at 3 mm and increases towards the top. For the „pomBasic MTI the diameter range starts at 0.2 mm and also increases towards the top.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1786",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Can larger tool diameters be measured with „pomBasic MTI can larger tool diameters also be measured?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The travel paths of the X and Y axes are identical for both device variants. This means that even larger tool diameters can be reliably measured with the „pomBasic MTI reliably measured.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1784",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Does ZOLLER offer for »pomBasic« and „pomBasic MTI tool holders?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>A large number of tool holders are available for a wide range of tool areas.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1782",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Why is there a CNC control for the camera axis?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Enables combined focus images of the tool, automatic camera positioning in relation to the tool surface and CNC-controlled movement of the camera axis using a joystick.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1803",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Why does the camera from the »pomBasic MTI« coaxial lighting and what is it?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The coaxial lighting is integrated directly into the camera system and ensures optimal, shadow-free lighting of the tool surface, especially for micro-tools.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1811",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      "ftype": "accordion",
      "id": "c1798",
      "bg": "",
      "space": {
       "before": "default",
       "after": "default"
      }
     }
    ]
